If the estimation takes 30min, but then 2h more for producing and summarising 10 posterior samples with predict()  is very odd!

Check how long generate(fit, n.samples=1) takes (I.e. with no predictor expression or newdata input). That only generates a joint sample from the model components. If that is quick, that would show that there’s a problem with your predictor data and/or expression, and I would probably need access to the data and code to debug it on my own system. (But as Haavard said, please upgrade to R 4.4 and the latest “testing” version of inla, to avoid debugging potentially already fixed issues in the older versions).

