for some models, like rw1, rw2, rankdef is known to be 1 for rw1 and 2 for rw2.

for 'generic0', then rankdef only enters in the normalizing constant as
prec^{(n-rankdef)/2}

the dimension of the singularity of 'generic0' is not computed

if you add m constraints, then rankdef is set to 'm' unless you say otherwise.

